{"name":"Wet Seal","hex":"#8a96a0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Perai."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made up of liquid or moisture, usually (but not always) water.","Of an object, etc.: covered or impregnated with liquid, usually (but not always) water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wet"},{"term":"seal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pinniped (Pinnipedia), particularly an earless seal (true seal) or eared seal."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt seals."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wet Seal","blocks":[{"text":"Wet Seal was an American fast fashion retailer, headquartered in Los Angeles, California. The retailer specialized in selling clothing and accessories. The company was founded in Newport Beach, California, by Lorne Huycke in 1962 as \"Lorne's\". The \"Wet Seal\" name is derived from a comment Huycke's wife made during a fashion show that a model wearing a bathing suit looked like a \"wet seal.\" The company was incorporated as Wet Seal in 1990."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Wetsealheadquarters.jpg/330px-Wetsealheadquarters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wet_Seal","wikidata":"Q7989983"},{"title":"Seal brown","blocks":[{"text":"Seal brown is a rich dark brown color, resembling the color of the dyed fur from the fur seal."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seal_brown","wikidata":"Q612837"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"wet":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9d/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-wet.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9d/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-wet.wav/LL-Q1